IMPORT prelude

-- Animals and Birds Act 1965 (Singapore) -- animal welfare and cruelty (Part 4: ss 41, 41B, 41C, 42, 43, 43A, 43B, 44(3)-(4),
-- 45(2), 46, 48), the owner's duty to report disease (s 30), the dog-bite production direction (s 39), compensation for destroyed
-- animals (ss 19(3), 20, 21, 40(12), 46), and composition (s 69).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ABA1965.txt ("version in
-- force from 1/3/2022"), with amendments to Act 23 of 2021 (s 42(1)(c), in force 1 March 2022) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a pet owner or an animal-related
-- business meets: the duty of care, cruelty, their penalties and the court's further orders. Not encoded: import, transhipment and
-- export licensing (ss 7-18), the disease-control powers of Part 3 other than s 30 and the compensation rules,
-- rabies orders (ss 37, 38, 40) except s 40(12), livestock control (Part 5), enforcement powers (Part 6), veterinary licensing
-- (Part 7), quarantine (Part 8), the content of any code of animal welfare, and every rule or order made under the Act (none was
-- retrieved -- in particular which offences are "prescribed as compoundable" under s 69 and which businesses are "prescribed" under
-- s 43).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Animals and Birds Act 1965 -- animal welfare`

§§ `41 -- animal-related business`

-- s 41: "animal-related business" means (a) operating a place for (i) "using or holding animals for display, sport, entertainment,
-- sale, breeding or conservation", or (ii) the care, boarding, grooming, treatment, vaccination, inoculation, training or
-- destruction of animals, "for reward"; (b) providing any such service (including transportation and capture) "for reward"; or
-- (c) "the operation of any animal rescue or welfare organisation or facility", "but does not include any business in respect of
-- animals intended for consumption". "Reward" means "any payment or other benefit (whether monetary or otherwise)".
-- INFERENCE: "for reward" is read as attaching to (a)(ii) and (b) only, so (a)(i) and (c) need no reward.
DECLARE Activity HAS
    `runs a place to display, sell, breed or conserve animals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cares for, boards, grooms, trains, treats or transports animals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `does it for reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `runs an animal rescue or welfare organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the animals are intended for consumption` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an animal-related business` IF
        (    `the activity`'s `runs a place to display, sell, breed or conserve animals`
         OR  (`the activity`'s `cares for, boards, grooms, trains, treats or transports animals` AND `the activity`'s `does it for reward`)
         OR  `the activity`'s `runs an animal rescue or welfare organisation`)
    AND (NOT `the activity`'s `the animals are intended for consumption`)

§§ `41B, 41C -- the owner's duty of care`

-- s 41C(1): every owner (which "includes a person in charge", s 41) (a) must take reasonable steps to ensure (i) adequate and
-- suitable food and water, (ii) adequate shelter, (iii) no confinement, conveying or handling causing "unreasonable or unnecessary
-- pain or suffering", (iv) protection from, and rapid diagnosis of, significant injury or disease; (b) must not abandon the animal,
-- "whether permanently or temporarily, without reasonable cause or excuse"; (c) if it is missing, "must make reasonable efforts to
-- recover the animal"; and (d) must take reasonable steps to ensure it is cared for in accordance with the codes of animal welfare.
-- s 41C(2): failure to comply with "subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c)" is an offence -- NOT (d).
-- s 41B(1): no criminal liability "by reason only" of failing to observe a code; (2) but a party may rely on compliance or
-- non-compliance "as tending to establish or negate any liability".
DECLARE OwnerConduct HAS
    `gave adequate and suitable food and water` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave adequate shelter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `avoided confinement or handling causing unnecessary suffering` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took reasonable steps against injury and disease` IS A BOOLEAN
    `abandoned the animal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had reasonable cause or excuse for leaving it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the animal went missing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made reasonable efforts to recover it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `followed the applicable code of animal welfare` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS AN OwnerConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner commits the duty-of-care offence` IF
        (NOT `the conduct`'s `gave adequate and suitable food and water`)
    OR  (NOT `the conduct`'s `gave adequate shelter`)
    OR  (NOT `the conduct`'s `avoided confinement or handling causing unnecessary suffering`)
    OR  (NOT `the conduct`'s `took reasonable steps against injury and disease`)
    OR  (`the conduct`'s `abandoned the animal` AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `had reasonable cause or excuse for leaving it`))
    OR  (`the conduct`'s `the animal went missing` AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `made reasonable efforts to recover it`))

-- The whole of s 41C(1), including (d). The difference between this and the offence is the code of animal welfare.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS AN OwnerConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner falls short of s 41C(1)` IF
        `the owner commits the duty-of-care offence` `the conduct`
    OR  (NOT `the conduct`'s `followed the applicable code of animal welfare`)

§§ `42 -- cruelty`

-- s 42(1): an offence for any person who (a) "cruelly beats, kicks, ill-treats, over-rides, over-drives, over-loads, tortures,
-- infuriates or terrifies any animal"; (b) "causes or procures or, being the owner, permits any animal to be so used"; (c) "by
-- rashly or unreasonably doing or omitting to do any act, causes any unnecessary pain or suffering" (Act 23 of 2021 wef 01/03/2022);
-- (d) employs in work an animal unfit for it by disease, infirmity, wound or sore; (e) causes, procures or assists at animal
-- fighting or baiting, or keeps or lets premises for it.
-- (2): "an owner is deemed to have permitted cruelty to an animal, if the owner has failed to exercise reasonable care and
-- supervision in respect of the animal".
-- (3): nothing applies to destruction or preparation for destruction "of any animal as food, unless that destruction or
-- preparation was accompanied by the infliction of unnecessary suffering".
-- s 41: in Part 4 "animal" includes "any beast, bird, fish or reptile, whether wild or tame".
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `was cruel to the animal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused or procured another to be cruel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another person was cruel to the animal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `failed to exercise reasonable care and supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rashly or unreasonably caused unnecessary pain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `worked an animal unfit for work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took part in animal fighting or baiting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was slaughtering the animal for food` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inflicted unnecessary suffering` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is listed in s 42(1)` IF
        `the conduct`'s `was cruel to the animal`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `caused or procured another to be cruel`
    OR  (    `the conduct`'s `is the owner`
         AND `the conduct`'s `another person was cruel to the animal`
         AND (`the conduct`'s `permitted it` OR `the conduct`'s `failed to exercise reasonable care and supervision`))
    OR  `the conduct`'s `rashly or unreasonably caused unnecessary pain`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `worked an animal unfit for work`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `took part in animal fighting or baiting`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the cruelty offence` IF
        `the conduct is listed in s 42(1)` `the conduct`
    AND (NOT (`the conduct`'s `was slaughtering the animal for food` AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `inflicted unnecessary suffering`)))

§§ `Penalties -- ss 30, 39, 41C(3), 42(4), 43(3), 43A(2), 48(2)`

-- s 41C(3): in the course of an animal-related business, first offence $40,000 or 2 years, second or subsequent $100,000 or 3
-- years; in any other case $10,000 or 12 months, then $20,000 or 2 years.
-- s 42(4): business -- the same $40,000 / 2 years and $100,000 / 3 years; any other case $15,000 or 18 months, then $30,000 or 3
-- years.
-- s 43(3): employing an unqualified individual in a prescribed business, $5,000 or 6 months.
-- s 43A(2): failing a Director-General's welfare direction without reasonable excuse, business $20,000 or 12 months; otherwise
-- $10,000 or 12 months.
-- s 48(2): keeping animals or birds in captivity "for sale, export or exhibition" in an unlicensed place, $5,000 or 6 months.
-- s 39(3): failing to produce a dog that has bitten a person, a fine not exceeding $2,000 (no imprisonment).
-- s 30(5): failing to report an animal infected or suspected to be infected with disease, $10,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `breach of the duty of care`
    `cruelty`
    `employing unqualified staff`
    `ignoring a welfare direction`
    `keeping animals for sale in an unlicensed place`
    `not producing a dog that bit someone`
    `not reporting a diseased animal`

GIVEN `cond` IS A BOOLEAN, `yes` IS A NUMBER, `no` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`pick` MEANS IF `cond` THEN `yes` ELSE `no`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `in a business` IS A BOOLEAN, `a repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breach of the duty of care` THEN `pick` `in a business` (`pick` `a repeat` 100000 40000) (`pick` `a repeat` 20000 10000)
    WHEN `cruelty` THEN `pick` `in a business` (`pick` `a repeat` 100000 40000) (`pick` `a repeat` 30000 15000)
    WHEN `employing unqualified staff` THEN 5000
    WHEN `ignoring a welfare direction` THEN `pick` `in a business` 20000 10000
    WHEN `keeping animals for sale in an unlicensed place` THEN 5000
    WHEN `not producing a dog that bit someone` THEN 2000
    WHEN `not reporting a diseased animal` THEN 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `in a business` IS A BOOLEAN, `a repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breach of the duty of care` THEN `pick` `in a business` (`pick` `a repeat` 36 24) (`pick` `a repeat` 24 12)
    WHEN `cruelty` THEN `pick` `in a business` (`pick` `a repeat` 36 24) (`pick` `a repeat` 36 18)
    WHEN `employing unqualified staff` THEN 6
    WHEN `ignoring a welfare direction` THEN 12
    WHEN `keeping animals for sale in an unlicensed place` THEN 6
    WHEN `not producing a dog that bit someone` THEN 0
    WHEN `not reporting a diseased animal` THEN 12

-- s 41C(4): "a person is a repeat offender if" convicted under s 41C(2) after at least one earlier conviction "of an offence under
-- section 42(1)(f) in force immediately before" 16 January 2015. But s 41C(3) speaks of a "second or subsequent offence" and never
-- uses the words "repeat offender". INFERENCE: (4) is read as making an old s 42(1)(f) conviction count as the first offence for
-- s 41C(3). Nothing in s 42 makes an old conviction count for cruelty.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `an earlier conviction for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `an earlier conviction under the old s 42(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a second or subsequent offence` IF
        `an earlier conviction for the same offence`
    OR  (    `an earlier conviction under the old s 42(1)(f)`
         AND CONSIDER `the offence`
             WHEN `breach of the duty of care` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `43B, 44(3)-(4) -- disqualification and loss of the animal`

-- s 43B(1): on conviction under "section 41C(2), 42(1) or 43(3)" the court may (a) in the business case disqualify the person
-- from carrying on an animal-related business or being in charge of animals in one, or (b) "in any other case, disqualify the
-- person from owning any animal", "for a period not exceeding 12 months". A s 43A direction offence does not qualify.
-- s 44(3): where an owner is convicted of "an offence under this Part", the court may deprive the owner of the animal; (4) but
-- only if "satisfied by evidence as to a previous conviction, or as to the character of the owner or otherwise, that the animal,
-- if left with the owner, is likely to be exposed to cruelty". Part 4 runs from s 41 to s 48; ss 30 and 39 are in Part 3.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may disqualify` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breach of the duty of care` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cruelty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `employing unqualified staff` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disqualification period is within the limit` IF `months` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `in a business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disqualification may bar owning any animal` IF NOT `in a business`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Part 4 offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not producing a dog that bit someone` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `not reporting a diseased animal` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the convicted person is the owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `the animal is likely to be exposed to cruelty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may take the animal from its owner` IF
        `is a Part 4 offence` `the offence`
    AND `the convicted person is the owner`
    AND `the animal is likely to be exposed to cruelty`

§§ `45(2) -- notice before a destruction direction`

-- s 45(1): an authorised officer or police officer satisfied that an animal's disease or injury is incurable "or that it is
-- cruel to keep the animal alive" may give written directions for its destruction. (2): if the animal is "in any house, stable,
-- shed, or enclosure proper for that animal and not in a public thoroughfare, market or place", directions "must not be given
-- until the owner of the animal (if known) has been duly notified".
GIVEN `incurable or cruel to keep alive` IS A BOOLEAN, `in its own enclosure off public places` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner is known` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner was notified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may direct destruction now` IF
        `incurable or cruel to keep alive`
    AND (    (NOT `in its own enclosure off public places`)
         OR  (NOT `the owner is known`)
         OR  `the owner was notified`)

§§ `19(3), 21, 40(12), 46 -- compensation for a destroyed animal`

-- s 19(3): none for an animal destroyed for examination. s 21(1): none for an animal destroyed under s 20 (isolation or
-- destruction of diseased animals), but (2) "Despite subsection (1), the Minister may authorise the payment of such sum as the
-- Minister may determine". s 40(12): none for a dog destroyed under the anti-rabies provisions. s 46: "No compensation is in any
-- case payable" for destruction under a court order (s 44(1)(c)), an officer's written directions (s 45(1)), or at the written
-- request of "any person professing to be the owner".
-- INFERENCE: s 21(2) is read as reaching s 20 destructions only; the text says "any animal or bird which has been destroyed".
DECLARE Destruction IS ONE OF
    `destroyed for a disease examination`
    `destroyed as diseased on an officer's requirement`
    `an unvaccinated dog destroyed under a rabies order`
    `destroyed by court order as incurable`
    `destroyed on an officer's directions as cruel to keep alive`
    `destroyed at the request of a professed owner`

GIVEN `the destruction` IS A Destruction, `the Minister authorises payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation is payable` IF
    CONSIDER `the destruction`
    WHEN `destroyed as diseased on an officer's requirement` THEN `the Minister authorises payment`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `30 -- reporting disease`

-- s 30(1): every owner or person in charge of an animal or bird "infected with or reasonably suspected to be infected with
-- disease" must "immediately" report to an authorised officer or the nearest police station and confine and isolate it and its
-- contacts. (2) a suspected disease death must be reported and the carcase not moved without written permission. (3) "It is not
-- an offence to bury the carcase of the animal, if no instructions have been received within 24 hours of making the report".
-- (5) failing to report "without reasonable excuse" is an offence.
GIVEN `infected or reasonably suspected` IS A BOOLEAN, `reported` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to report disease is an offence` IF
    `infected or reasonably suspected` AND (NOT `reported`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

-- Exactly 24 hours is not asserted: "within 24 hours" leaves the boundary open.
GIVEN `hours since the report` IS A NUMBER, `instructions received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `burying the carcase is not an offence` IF
    `hours since the report` GREATER THAN 24 AND (NOT `instructions received`)

§§ `69 -- composition`

-- s 69(1): the Director-General or an authorised officer may compound "any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding $1,000". (2) on payment, no further proceedings. Which offences are
-- prescribed is in rules not retrieved.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum` AT MOST 1000
